{
  "meta": {},
  "name": "Sync Lemlist email & LinkedIn activity to Breakcold CRM and log events to Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "fc5ae8ff-5780-4223-ac68-ca10c5631cbb",
      "name": "Sticky: Template Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1856,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 796,
        "height": 1100,
        "content": "## Sync Lemlist email & LinkedIn activity to Breakcold CRM and log every event to Google Sheets\n\nOutbound agencies and sales teams running campaigns in **Lemlist** can use this workflow to push every email and LinkedIn touchpoint (sends, opens, clicks, replies, bounces, invites accepted and more) to the matching lead's timeline in **Breakcold** in real time. Every event is also logged to a **Google Sheet**, giving you a full audit trail of campaign engagement and flagging events that could not be synced, so gaps get fixed instead of lost.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Receive Lemlist events:** a webhook catches each Lemlist activity event as it happens.\n2. **Normalize the payload:** extracts event type, timestamp, lead email, campaign, sequence step and the custom variables `breakcold_lead_id` and `contact_id`, handling varying field names and timestamp formats.\n3. **Filter & secure:** drops non-lead events and (optionally) verifies a shared webhook secret.\n4. **Route by event type:** 12 email and LinkedIn events are recognized. Anything else is logged as unrecognized.\n5. **Post to Breakcold:** if the lead has a Breakcold ID, the event is added as a custom activity on their timeline (e.g. \"emailsReplied (Lemlist)\") with campaign, step, email and the original event time.\n6. **Log to Google Sheets:** every event becomes a row with timestamp, contact, campaign, client, channel, event type, step, a `matched` flag and an `error` reason (`no_breakcold_id`, `unrecognized_event_type` or the Breakcold error code). Breakcold failures never stop the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\n- Lemlist account with API/webhook access\n- Breakcold account and API key\n- Google account with Google Sheets\n\n### Setup steps (15 to 20 min)\n1. **Breakcold credential:** in *Breakcold: Post Custom Activity*, create a **Header Auth** credential. Name: `Authorization`, Value: `Bearer YOUR_BREAKCOLD_API_KEY` (the `Bearer ` prefix is required, otherwise Breakcold rejects the call).\n2. **Google Sheets:** create a spreadsheet with a tab named `Events` and these headers in row 1: `timestamp, contact_id, campaign_id, client, channel, event_type, sequence_step, matched, error`. In *Append to Google Sheets (Events)*, connect your Google account and pick the spreadsheet.\n3. **Lemlist custom variables:** give each lead a `breakcold_lead_id` variable (the Breakcold record ID) and optionally `contact_id` (your own internal ID, e.g. from Clay or your CRM).\n4. **Config:** open *Normalize Event* and set `CLIENT_NAME` (and optionally `SECRET`) at the top of the code.\n5. **Lemlist webhook:** activate the workflow, copy the **Production URL** from *Lemlist Webhook* and add it in Lemlist (Settings > Integrations > Webhooks) for the email and LinkedIn events you want to track.\n6. **Test:** trigger an event (e.g. send a test email) and check Breakcold and the sheet."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2b5fa5bd-d2f8-4724-921f-bfaefd54187d",
      "name": "Sticky: Normalize Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -800,
        416
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 540,
        "height": 596,
        "content": "## Normalize Event: config & payload mapping\n\n**Edit only the CONFIG block** at the top of the code:\n- `CLIENT_NAME`: written to the `client` column. Useful if you run this workflow for several clients or workspaces.\n- `SECRET`: optional. If you add a secret to the Lemlist webhook, paste the same value here and requests without it are dropped. Leave empty to disable.\n\n**Lemlist notes**\n- `sequenceStep` is **zero-indexed** (step 1 in the Lemlist UI arrives as `0`).\n- The code checks several possible field paths for each value (e.g. `customVariables.*`, flat body fields, `lead.*`). If your payloads differ, adjust the paths here only. Every downstream node reads from this node's output.\n- If you subscribe to Lemlist's grouped lead-state events (contacted / hooked / warmed etc.) in addition to the granular ones, the same activity may arrive twice. Grouped events are logged as `unrecognized_event_type`, so you can see them and unsubscribe if you don't need them."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ce07c75a-9f08-4f10-a8b9-9faa5d9c28cd",
      "name": "Sticky: Breakcold Sync",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        32,
        -176
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 764,
        "height": 704,
        "content": "## Breakcold sync & error handling\n\n- **Endpoint:** `POST https://rest.breakcold.com/api/v1/records/{breakcold_lead_id}/custom-activities`\n- **Auth:** Header Auth credential, header `Authorization`, value `Bearer YOUR_API_KEY`\n- **Body:** `title`, `descriptionPlain` and `startAt` (Unix time in **milliseconds**, as a number)\n- **Rate limit:** 120 requests/min per route. The node retries 3 times with a 2 s wait.\n\n**Error handling:** the HTTP node uses *Continue (using error output)*. A failed Breakcold call does **not** stop the workflow. The event is still written to Google Sheets with `matched = false` and the Breakcold error code in the `error` column, so you can filter the sheet and replay missed events.\n\nTo change what appears on the Breakcold timeline, edit the JSON body of *Breakcold: Post Custom Activity*."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "62443166-b493-482f-b990-0234036caa82",
      "name": "Lemlist Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "position": [
        -976,
        272
      ],
      "webhookId": "74c9d571-d643-4ba7-8d6f-8996efcaafd6",
      "parameters": {
        "path": "lemlist-events",
        "options": {},
        "httpMethod": "POST"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.1
    },
    {
      "id": "a880035f-3e4e-415a-bd38-57847d99f36b",
      "name": "Normalize Event",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        -752,
        272
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// ===== CONFIG: edit these two values =====\nconst SECRET = '';                     // Optional: same secret you set on the Lemlist webhook. Empty = check disabled\nconst CLIENT_NAME = 'YOUR_CLIENT_NAME'; // Written to the \"client\" column in Google Sheets\n// ==========================================\nconst results = [];\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\n  const body = item.json.body || {};\n  const headers = item.json.headers || {};\n  const query = item.json.query || {};\n  const lead = body.lead || {};\n  const eventType = body.type || body.event || body.eventType || '';\n  const rawTimestamp = body.createdAt || body.timestamp || body.date || null;\n  let occurredAtMs;\n  if (rawTimestamp !== null && rawTimestamp !== undefined && rawTimestamp !== '') {\n    const num = Number(rawTimestamp);\n    if (!isNaN(num)) {\n      occurredAtMs = num < 1+1234567890 ? num * 1000 : num;\n    } else {\n      const parsed = Date.parse(rawTimestamp);\n      occurredAtMs = isNaN(parsed) ? Date.now() : parsed;\n    }\n  } else {\n    occurredAtMs = Date.now();\n  }\n  const leadEmail = body.leadEmail || body.email || lead.email || '';\n  const campaignId = body.campaignId || body._campaignId || '';\n  const campaignName = body.campaignName || '';\n  // NOTE: Lemlist sequenceStep/totalSequenceStep are ZERO-indexed (per docs)\n  const sequenceStep = body.sequenceStep ?? body.emailTemplate ?? body.stepIndex ?? '';\n  const customVars = body.customVariables || body.customFields || body.customVariable || {};\n  const contactId = customVars.contact_id || body.contact_id || lead.contact_id\n    || customVars.clay_contact_id || body.clay_contact_id || lead.clay_contact_id || '';\n  const breakcoldId = customVars.breakcold_lead_id || body.breakcold_lead_id || lead.breakcold_lead_id || '';\n  const secret = headers['x-lemlist-secret'] || headers['x-webhook-secret'] || headers['secret'] || body.secret || query.secret || '';\n  const secretOk = !SECRET || secret === SECRET;\n  results.push({ json: {\n    event_type: eventType,\n    occurred_at_ms: occurredAtMs,\n    lead_email: leadEmail,\n    campaign_id: campaignId,\n    campaign_name: campaignName,\n    sequence_step: sequenceStep,\n    contact_id: contactId,\n    breakcold_id: breakcoldId,\n    client: CLIENT_NAME,\n    secret_ok: secretOk,\n    raw: body\n  } });\n}\nreturn results;"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
